{"evidence_ref":"legacy-resolved-catalog-v0:object:2418","export_status":"complete","facet_counts":{"attributes":0,"displays":0,"inlets":3,"outlets":2,"parameters":8,"ports":5},"legacy_class":"axoloti.object.AxoObject","legacy_id":"sss/filter/mostFilter3","legacy_kind":"native_definition","metadata":{"author":"Remco van der Most","description":"My own filter, with a filtering based on the workings of \"gravity\".\nThis version has limiters/distortions added in both the normal filter path as well as the \"resonance\" path (the rate at which the filter can respond) and also just before the filter to prevent errors caused by \"too hot levels\".\n-first stage: soft-clipping (native soft-distortion algorithm)\n-second stage: adding an extra 6dB LP-filter. Note though, that this has another effect when in HP-mode, actually adding back bass to the HP-filter because of phase-differences caused by the 2-sample delay.\n-third stage: calculating the rate-in/decrease based on input and current filter position\n-fourth stage: limiting the rate\n-fifth stage: applying rate to filter\n-sixth stage: limiting the filter\n-seventh stage: optionally adding inversed input signal to filter to get HP-mode.\n\nThe \"treshold\" limiter is a hard-clipper.\nThe \"drive\" subtracts a 3rd degree power from the signal to limit it's range. Because of the curve, it has a bit softer distortion then the hard limiter.","help_patch":null,"license":"BSD"},"origin":{"definition_index":0,"generated_by":null,"kind":"file","path":"objects/sss/filter/mostfilter3.axo","source_id":"axoloti-contrib"},"rank_sha256":"002f6c09d28b4785580c06bca851870e03320d8abacb510a83f5dd2e443533b9","schema_version":"phase3-review-object-sample-v0","selection_stage":"fill","stratum":"file|native_definition|axoloti-contrib","uuid":{"durable_value":"e589f268-1c81-4b21-9a1d-ef2fa2a5713a","runtime_kind":"explicit","source_presence":"present","source_value":"e589f268-1c81-4b21-9a1d-ef2fa2a5713a"},"variant_index":2418}
